  "_comment": "The in-universe ads (docs/channel.md §16.11; Task 105, Tom's picks from ads.html, Task 94). Each gap between live matches shuffles them into its own seeded order (Task 158), its breaks taking settings.ads.perBreak at a time, each carrying on where the last stopped (1-3, 4-6, ...); the stills take a fresh shuffle each pass. The order here is only for reading. Each: id, brand and product, the region it's from, its tagline, colours (the brand name's fill and edge on its end card), scene (which drawn ad it is: the brands' in src/channel/adBrands.js, the league's own in adLeague.js) effects (Task 205: the ad's small sounds, musicRecipes.js effectLayers, each at its moment in seconds, a gain to soften one), and a jingle: a few notes (MIDI note numbers, lengths in beats) on one of the anthems' instruments (brass, organ, bells) at bpm, starting `at` seconds into the ad, as its brand comes up. Tickets and Season tickets (Task 146) are the league's own ads; their facts (the next live match; a team, seeded per break, and the season on sale) come from the league. The playoffs promo is the channel's own, not an ad: its brand is the event, its times come from the calendar.",
